    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83620.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "Well, look, look, breaking the law, high crimes and misdemeanors. There are a lot of members of Congress that know that the president is flouting the law. He knows that he's a field that he's generally incompetent and so on and so forth. But they're waiting for a violation of section and code. And if we find that violation, in fact, then those indeed are undeniably impeachable offense. And now I will tell you, that impeachment, as far as we know it for presidents, judges, those type of things, is not a legal remedy. It is a political remedy, yet some of my colleagues are not convinced of that. The political remedy already exists. We need to convince some of our colleagues that the legal remedy exists, if indeed it does. And right now, that looks like that's where we're headed.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
